# Written fresh for D:\Dev\momentum (M001 §2). Not carried from momentum-harness.
#
# EVERY RULE HERE IS ANCHORED with a leading slash unless it genuinely must match
# at any depth. The old repo's rules were unanchored -- `*.jsonl`, `*.zst` and
# `*.parquet` matched at any depth and would silently swallow a provenance
# companion or a ledger, so a file looked committed right up until the day
# someone went looking for it. That trap needed a negation block and a test to
# undo. Anchoring is the fix that does not need undoing.

# Claude Code config. NEVER tracked -- M001 §6: "Do not copy .claude/ in any
# form", and the old tree's .claude/settings.local.json held a Databento key.
.claude/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# Credentials never live in the tree - read them from the environment.
# tests/test_no_secrets.py enforces this; these lines are the first defence.
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
secrets.yaml

# Market data is large and licensed - never commit it. Anchored: a file named
# `notes.zst` inside an evidence folder is not market data.
/raw/
/bars/
/cache/
/selection/
*.dbn
*.dbn.zst

# Local append-only run state, carried as evidence but not tracked. The payloads
# are large and regenerable-in-shape; the LEDGERS are not, and those are tracked
# (see EVIDENCE-CARRY.md).
/records/
/records_truncated/

# The adoption drop folder lives outside both repos (D:\Dev\_adopt\) and is
# never committed. This line is belt-and-braces in case one is made in-tree.
/_adopt/

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
